TensorFold patch 0101 (this recipe's first): Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (qwen3_5_moe) from an EXL3 pack on CUDA.

Why: TensorFold 0.6.5 serves Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on CUDA from MLX 4-bit weights only ("NVFP4 and EXL3 exports of it are
not read yet", docs/recipes/qwen3.6-moe.md; family check() refused any other format). The 27B's EXL3 loader
(qwen3_5/cuda/exl3_load.py) already reads the same DeltaNet / attention layers, and the shared EXL3 grouped expert
kernels (cuda/exl3/experts.py, Flash Next's) read routed experts at any width; nothing joined them for this family.

What:
- families/qwen3_5_moe/cuda/exl3.py (new): Exl3Routed, a layer's router rows [256 + 1, D] (the shared expert's gate
  row last, as the MLX path) and its 256 experts plus the shared expert as expert 256 in one EXL3 table (read with
  Flash Next's expert_table / Pack). Routing is tensorfold.cuda.moe's (fp32 logits, top 8 renormalized, sigmoid
  shared gate); the weighted slot sum runs in fp32 in slot order (down_combine / down_sum) and is rounded once to
  bf16, moe.run's contract. Verify rows (<= 128) use the grouped decode kernel (row-invariant: drafted replies equal
  serial ones); prompt chunks the prompt kernel (chunk-invariant, as every EXL3 prompt matmul). One routing scratch
  for all layers (4096 rows: a prompt chunk), counted by the admission.
  load(): the 27B's load_exl3 for everything but the MLPs, each MLP an Exl3Routed. load_mtp(): the pack's own MTP
  layer (mtp.*, EXL3 4-bit in ExLlamaV3 >= 1.4 packs): fc kept whole over [embedding | hidden], norms +1 (stored as
  gamma - 1 like the pack's other norms), its experts an Exl3Routed whose prompt-length rows (the head absorbing a
  prompt) take the prompt kernel. draft_head(): the EXL3 head's rows for the draft vocabulary decoded once and
  requantized to MLX 4-bit g64 (drafts only choose rows to verify, never output bits). admission(): tensors as stored
  (vision tower skipped, MTP counted when drafting) plus the expert and prompt-matmul scratch.
- cuda/moe.py run(): a layer whose experts are not MLX Routed runs its own run(x, prefill=...) (one line).
- qwen3_5/cuda/exl3_load.py load_exl3(moe=None): with moe, a MoE pack's .mlp. tensors are left to that hook and each
  layer gets moe=hook(prefix). The 27B (moe=None) loads exactly as before.
- qwen3_5_moe/cuda/weights.py: load() / load_mtp() take the EXL3 path for an EXL3 pack (MLX checkpoints unchanged; an
  mtp-4bit.safetensors side file still wins for the MTP layer). MTP gets an optional whole `fc`.
- qwen3_5_moe/cuda/mtp.py: the head's embedding through glue.embedding (an EXL3 pack's bf16 table; the MLX table
  dequantizes as before), its projections through forward._mm (MLX words: the same qmm_fast.matmul call as before),
  fc whole when the MTP layer has one, the draft head from draft_head() when the target head is EXL3.
- qwen3_5_moe/cuda/engine.py: the EXL3 admission; `keep` (prompt states the concurrent decoder keeps; default 3 as
  before) from --checkpoint-slots.
- qwen3_5_moe/__init__.py: QUANT_METHODS cuda (mlx, exl3), EXL3_VARIANT any, CUDA_CHECKPOINT_SLOTS; check() lets an
  EXL3 pack through (its tensors are checked by the loader); cuda_engine passes checkpoint_slots.
- tests/cuda/test_qwen36_exl3_moe.py: window independence of verify rows and prompt rows, prompt vs decode kernel,
  the MTP layer's wide rows on the prompt kernel.

Not done: images (the 35B's CUDA engine has no vision path in 0.6.5, MLX or EXL3; the pack's bf16 tower is unused).

Base: TensorFold 609ca419 + the Flash recipe's vision-prefix-cache.patch + 0001-0005 (copies of the Flash
recipe's local patches).

